<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    An MSVC __cdecl import's by-value class argument is sized at the call site
    (`option msvcbyval on|off`).

    Issue: GH Noelo-Lab/kuna#990. An MSVC name states every parameter's type but
    not the size of a class passed by value, so msvcsig applies such an import's
    parameters up to the class and leaves the rest open. MSVC copy-constructs the
    class in its outgoing slot (`push ecx; mov ecx,esp; call ??0`), so the
    call-site recovery refuses every slot from that address up, and the call
    keeps only the parameters before the class.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 callee-prototype (`p4_calls/kuna_msvcbyval.rs`, run at
    the end of ActionDefaultParams on the raw p-code) feeding P3 heritage (the
    constructor call creates the slot) and P6 ActionRestrictLocal (the slot
    stays a mapped local).

    P0 assertion: `option msvcbyval on|off` (on by default; inert without
    msvcsig).

    Fixtures (see the fixtures README):
      msvcsig_protos_i386.exe 0x401020, the issue's repro:
        Arr Build(Arr &x, Arr &y) { return MakeStack(x, x, y); }
        with ?MakeStack@@YA?AVArr@@V1@AAV1@1@Z, `add esp,0x10` after the call.
      msvcbyval_i386.exe:
        0x401000 void Wide(Pair &p) { Join(p, p); }   8-byte Pair, `sub esp,8`
        0x401020 Late: Note(1)'s pop deferred into MakeStack's `add esp,0x14`
        0x401050 Folded: no frame pointer, the cleanup also releases a local
                 (MakeStack(y, x, y) into a local r)

    Pass 1 (`option msvcbyval off`) is the BUG: MakeStack(a1) and Join() keep
    only the parameters before the class, and the pushed `ecx` that reserves
    the slot is an extra parameter of Build.
    Pass 2 (default) is the FIX: MakeStack(a0,v1,a1,a2) and Join(v1,a0), the
    copy constructor building that same local, and Build taking exactly its
    three parameters. Late and Folded must stay as they were: their cleanups
    over-state MakeStack's arguments, so the size is declined (two of each).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
